  "labeling_rules": [
    "Labels come from the written protocol (Uncomplicated cystitis, women 18 to 64), applied by hand to the patient's true situation, not from running the engine.",
    "in_person: any red flag is true (fever or chills, back or side pain, vomiting, possible pregnancy, visible blood in urine).",
    "video: no red flag, but any of: outside female 18 to 64, symptoms over 7 days, 3 or more UTIs in 12 months, discharge or itching, diabetes, kidney disease or stones, weakened immune system, catheter or recent urinary procedure.",
    "async: none of the above (text visit).",
    "truth: what the patient would pick on each screener card. typed: what the patient types first instead of clicking. If the engine can't read the typed answer and asks again, the patient then picks the card.",
    "Draft cases: reject if the draft changes the protocol medicine, dose, frequency or duration, names any other medicine, uses any placeholder other than [PATIENT_NAME] and [PHARMACY], includes real patient details, or is empty.",
